BAR Droid phone version of BAR's Tooltip (luaui/widgets/gui_tooltip.lua): a line wider than the screen wrapped to it.
BAR's tooltip moves a box that would run past the screen's right edge to the pointer's left, but never wraps a line;
its callers wrap their text by the font's size (80 characters and the like), and the font is sized by the screen's
height, so upright on a phone a tooltip's lines are wider than the screen and run off it (dev phone, 2026-11-15: the
Widget Selector's row tooltips cut at the right edge). Applied by the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's file as
LuaUI loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file runs. (Since BAR test-31958: the text it measures is
`text`, the value or its content's text.)

@@@ find
			lines = string_lines(text)
			for i, line in ipairs(lines) do
@@@ with
			lines = string_lines(text)
			-- BAR Droid (phone): a line wider than the screen (less the box's padding) wrapped to it
			local fit = vsx - (paddingW * 4)
			local wrapped = {}
			for _, line in ipairs(lines) do
				if fit > 0 and font:GetTextWidth(line) * fontSize > fit then
					for part in (font:WrapText(line, fit, nil, fontSize) .. "\n"):gmatch("(.-)\n") do
						wrapped[#wrapped + 1] = part
					end
				else
					wrapped[#wrapped + 1] = line
				end
			end
			lines = wrapped
			for i, line in ipairs(lines) do
@@@ end
